                <pb facs="0639" n="515" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg515"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.102 Ic/22: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Ruddock</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-08-23T22:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 23,
                                1921—10 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received August 24—6:52
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>295. My 288, August 16th, 5 p.m. Diplomatic body today accepted Department’s
                    proposals with the proviso that they may apply retroactively to Ichang and
                    Wuchang mutinies and on understanding <pb facs="0640" n="516" xml:id="pg516"/>
                    that diplomatic body as a whole will support claims for punitive damages of the
                    nationals of a particular country injured by proscribed official. Does
                    Department approve? Dean of the diplomatic corps delaying note to Foreign
                    Office. Requests your reply within three days.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ruddock</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
